WEBVTT

00:06.340 --> 00:08.460
What’s wrong, Itsumi?

00:08.460 --> 00:09.860
A call from the President?

00:10.450 --> 00:11.800
Yes, this is Mamoru.

00:12.750 --> 00:14.900
A message from Ayako-san’s grandfather?

00:16.370 --> 00:18.950
“Get some swimming trunks”?!

00:36.140 --> 00:41.260
Today I shout out another good morning courageously

00:41.260 --> 00:46.560
The sparkling chime of hope is resounding

00:47.050 --> 00:52.140
The gentle sun is always

00:52.140 --> 00:57.660
Blessing the late coming sensation of the two of them

00:57.950 --> 01:02.880
To fall in love with a goddess is the best!

01:03.090 --> 01:12.950
Even if she is a beatrice I can't control this throbbing feeling

01:12.950 --> 01:13.800
L·O·V·E

01:13.800 --> 01:15.550
I love you MA·MO·RU!

01:15.550 --> 01:17.090
These overflowing feelings

01:17.090 --> 01:19.790
Take them high into the sky

01:19.790 --> 01:24.680
Please grant me my dazzling and sparkling dream

01:24.680 --> 01:26.480
That's right MA·MO·RU!

01:26.480 --> 01:28.010
Only for you

01:28.010 --> 01:30.680
I will show you my power of miracles

01:30.680 --> 01:32.950
I will surely, surely swear

01:32.950 --> 01:38.900
I will not end my Shining Love

01:57.020 --> 01:58.590
Reading a book?

01:59.320 --> 02:00.140
Yes.

02:00.980 --> 02:05.650
This is a book by the first scientist
to discover beatrice, ten years ago.

02:06.100 --> 02:08.210
I’ve read it many times since I was a kid.

02:08.700 --> 02:10.360
I never get tired of it.

02:10.360 --> 02:12.800
The one who discovered beatrice?

02:12.800 --> 02:17.630
Yes. A biologist and the strongest beatrice user.

02:17.630 --> 02:22.410
But her identity is unknown...

02:19.960 --> 02:21.790
To Takasu Masaki
Gertrude Macvilieze

02:24.610 --> 02:27.110
Gertrude Macvilieze.

02:27.110 --> 02:30.680
Also know as the Silver Maria.

02:35.570 --> 02:38.640
Jeez... Damn that old woman.

02:43.860 --> 02:48.090
Watch Out on the Tropical Island

02:48.090 --> 02:49.330
Don’t fall!

02:49.330 --> 02:50.540
Don’t drop!

02:50.540 --> 02:51.460
That’s right!

03:01.260 --> 03:04.700
A true man is one who stands up from defeat!

03:09.160 --> 03:13.400
Brother, this was great of Grandfather Naoyuki wasn’t it?

03:13.400 --> 03:15.980
Y-Yes... As an apology for

03:15.130 --> 03:21.130
A victory won after standing from the brink
of despair is the true proof of a man!

03:15.980 --> 03:21.130
the whole engagement thing, he’s sending
us all on a trip to a tropical island.

03:21.130 --> 03:22.720
Oh, Naoyuki-sensei!

03:22.720 --> 03:25.750
We need to thank Mamoru-kun.

03:25.750 --> 03:27.250
That’s right!

03:27.250 --> 03:29.520
P-President, Shione-san...

03:34.030 --> 03:35.260
Ayako-san?

03:36.110 --> 03:40.710
Eternal Love
Comes True

03:36.950 --> 03:40.240
Rainbow Cape, where eternal love comes true.

03:40.240 --> 03:44.080
It’s said that couples who kiss while
watching the rainbows here

03:44.080 --> 03:46.740
will have their love last forever...

03:47.820 --> 03:49.400
<i>Ayako-san...</i>

03:49.400 --> 03:50.980
<i>Mamoru...</i>

03:51.670 --> 03:52.810
<i>Ayako-san.</i>

03:54.730 --> 03:55.810
Ayako-san?

03:59.930 --> 04:01.760
M-M-Mamoru?

04:02.270 --> 04:04.760
Let’s go see the Rainbow Cape together.

04:05.780 --> 04:06.940
Yeah...

04:10.990 --> 04:12.630
It has to be a secret from everyone.

04:12.630 --> 04:14.120
We need to be alone.

04:14.120 --> 04:15.030
Right.

04:15.030 --> 04:16.760
But I don’t know if we’ll get the chance.

04:16.760 --> 04:17.940
We will.

04:17.940 --> 04:20.140
I’ll beat up anyone who gets in our way.

04:21.210 --> 04:23.100
Just the two of us, Mamoru!

04:23.100 --> 04:24.980
R-Right, Ayako-san!

04:38.350 --> 04:40.450
W-W-Well?

04:40.450 --> 04:43.170
What do you think, Mamoru?

04:45.450 --> 04:47.440
Big wave!

04:47.950 --> 04:51.370
You idiots!

04:51.370 --> 04:54.140
You guys always...

04:54.890 --> 04:56.810
Why me, too?!

05:02.990 --> 05:06.920
Jeez... Those guys really...

05:06.920 --> 05:08.910
Always, always, always...

05:09.270 --> 05:11.730
I was finally, finally...

05:11.730 --> 05:14.100
It’s very cute.

05:14.750 --> 05:19.600
A-And you’re so pretty, really.

05:21.000 --> 05:21.910
Mamoru!

05:21.910 --> 05:24.910
Wonderful, huh, Ayako?

05:24.910 --> 05:27.020
He said he likes it!

05:27.020 --> 05:28.920
It was worth all that...

05:28.920 --> 05:30.870
time spent at the shop!

05:30.870 --> 05:32.310
E-Everyone...

05:32.310 --> 05:34.650
She ended up buying a bunch,

05:34.650 --> 05:37.200
and she was still choosing until she left the hotel.

05:37.200 --> 05:39.360
Oh, that’s Emelenzia-san!

05:39.640 --> 05:40.790
Oh, my!

05:43.200 --> 05:44.930
That’s wrong, Brother!

05:44.930 --> 05:46.880
Hitting on Emelenzia-san!

05:46.880 --> 05:47.740
That’s right!

05:47.740 --> 05:49.690
That’s not something a student
council president should do!

05:49.690 --> 05:52.050
I’m going to publish the photo!

05:52.050 --> 05:53.360
D-Don’t be stupid.

05:53.360 --> 05:54.140
I was just...

05:54.140 --> 05:56.000
Anyway, Emeleniza-kun...

05:56.000 --> 05:57.480
Are you not going to swim?

05:57.480 --> 05:59.450
Of course you can swim, right?

05:59.450 --> 06:01.260
Did you not bring your swimsuit?

06:01.260 --> 06:03.100
N-No, that isn’t it...

06:03.100 --> 06:04.830
Is it your girl’s day?

06:04.830 --> 06:06.790
People will get suspicious if you skip for three days.

06:06.790 --> 06:08.250
What is she talking about?

06:08.250 --> 06:11.440
Maybe she’s wearing a swimsuit under it?

06:11.440 --> 06:11.840
Yes...

06:11.840 --> 06:12.710
I see.

06:12.710 --> 06:13.530
Then...

06:13.530 --> 06:14.720
Right...

06:14.720 --> 06:16.670
Take it off!

06:16.670 --> 06:17.270
W-Wait!

06:17.270 --> 06:19.160
We won’t wait!

06:19.160 --> 06:20.400
No, I...

06:20.400 --> 06:23.030
Stop it, please!

06:26.250 --> 06:27.860
Th-This is...

06:27.860 --> 06:29.450
Emelenzia-san...

06:29.450 --> 06:30.930
B-Bold.

06:30.930 --> 06:32.320
Wow...

06:32.320 --> 06:33.910
It’ll make a good photo.

06:35.790 --> 06:43.400
Th-The salesperson s-said this
would be really p-popular...

06:43.400 --> 06:43.960
Oh, excuse me.

06:43.960 --> 06:44.660
Lovely!

06:46.760 --> 06:47.860
Nice job!

07:00.150 --> 07:01.770
Yoshimura Mamoru,

07:01.770 --> 07:03.000
you’ve let your guard down.

07:03.000 --> 07:04.830
You’ve let your guard down!

07:04.830 --> 07:07.190
I’ll wait for the right moment,

07:07.190 --> 07:10.700
and then I’ll take my beloved Ayako-san from your clutches.

07:10.700 --> 07:13.720
Watch over me, Naoyuki-sensei!

07:18.360 --> 07:19.920
Excuse me!

07:22.690 --> 07:24.280
Thank you!

07:41.440 --> 07:43.980
It can’t be helped.

07:43.980 --> 07:45.860
It was the result of a fair
rock-paper-scissors match.

07:45.860 --> 07:46.670
Give it up.

07:47.130 --> 07:49.650
You’re cute when you’re grouchy.

07:55.700 --> 07:57.210
<i>Why?</i>

07:57.210 --> 07:59.220
<i>Back then, why did I...</i>

07:59.750 --> 08:01.970
Hang on tight!

08:08.380 --> 08:09.300
Mamoru!

08:13.180 --> 08:14.650
Yoshimura!

08:16.270 --> 08:17.410
Mamoru-san!

08:17.410 --> 08:19.580
Are you OK, Mamoru-kun?

08:19.580 --> 08:22.300
Yes, I’m fine.

08:23.240 --> 08:24.450
Where’s Emelenzia?

08:26.800 --> 08:29.010
Emelenzia, are you OK?

08:29.010 --> 08:30.530
Yes, I’m fine.

08:30.530 --> 08:32.350
Don’t worry.

08:38.430 --> 08:40.500
Don’t come any closer.

08:40.500 --> 08:41.720
What’s wrong? Are you hurt?

08:44.570 --> 08:45.940
What should we do?

08:46.590 --> 08:47.910
Emelenzia!

08:49.370 --> 08:50.250
Ayako-san!

08:50.760 --> 08:52.730
What are you...

08:52.730 --> 08:54.590
No, this is...

08:55.430 --> 08:57.010
Don’t look, Mamoru!

08:57.010 --> 08:59.270
No, no, no!

08:59.270 --> 09:00.290
What?

09:06.620 --> 09:09.990
I’m sorry for the trouble!

09:12.990 --> 09:15.000
You really couldn’t see, right?

09:15.600 --> 09:17.040
Really!

09:17.040 --> 09:19.510
I looked away the second I saw her
bathing suit had fallen off.

09:19.510 --> 09:22.550
And the surface of the water was shining, so it was really hard to see what was underneath.

09:22.550 --> 09:23.730
Whatever.

09:23.730 --> 09:24.860
It was an accident.

09:24.860 --> 09:25.870
Y-Yeah...

09:26.310 --> 09:32.550
A-Anyway, Shione and the others left...

09:33.420 --> 09:35.200
Right, that’s true.

09:35.200 --> 09:36.510
Then...

09:41.670 --> 09:43.780
Naoyuki’s rules of street fighting.

09:43.780 --> 09:46.490
Don’t take your eyes off the enemy.
Grab the chance when you see it!

09:46.490 --> 09:47.400
I’ll do it!

09:47.400 --> 09:50.110
I’ll do it, Naoyuki-sensei!

09:50.110 --> 09:51.610
Oh, Abiko-sempai!

09:51.610 --> 09:52.710
Hey...

09:53.460 --> 09:55.570
Oh, Ayako and Mamoru-kun!

09:56.120 --> 09:57.420
E-Everyone.

09:57.420 --> 09:58.550
Where have you been?

09:58.550 --> 10:00.230
Oh, we went...

10:00.230 --> 10:04.330
Oh my, were the two of you going somewhere?

10:05.440 --> 10:08.960
Taking a walk on the beach while the sun sets?

10:09.930 --> 10:11.810
Romantic!

10:11.810 --> 10:15.650
But the tropical seas embolden young lovers!

10:15.650 --> 10:17.570
I hope it ends up being nothing more than romantic...

10:17.570 --> 10:18.410
Th-That’s wrong.

10:18.410 --> 10:21.150
No, we’re not...

10:21.150 --> 10:23.310
We’re not going anywhere!

10:24.180 --> 10:26.140
Really!

10:29.920 --> 10:32.870
Jeez, all of them...

10:32.870 --> 10:35.880
Well, we don’t leave for two days.

10:35.880 --> 10:37.540
That’s right! Tomorrow is our chance.

10:37.540 --> 10:38.490
Yes.

10:46.250 --> 10:46.930
Here you go.

10:47.540 --> 10:49.080
Thank you.

10:49.080 --> 10:51.200
You can speak Japanese.

10:51.200 --> 10:54.470
Yes, but just a little.

10:54.470 --> 10:56.280
I’m Mamoru.

10:56.280 --> 10:57.640
This is...

10:57.640 --> 10:58.480
Ayako.

10:58.480 --> 10:59.310
Nice to meet you.

10:59.310 --> 11:01.420
I am Mary.

11:01.420 --> 11:03.390
Nice to meet you!

11:06.290 --> 11:08.320
Time for good girls to go to sleep.

11:08.320 --> 11:11.730
When you get older, staying up late
will be bad for your skin.

11:11.730 --> 11:13.270
Better be careful.

11:14.020 --> 11:16.650
You aren’t that young, either.

11:17.120 --> 11:18.730
Your stomach’s sticking out.

11:22.970 --> 11:23.960
Old man!

11:30.220 --> 11:32.000
Damned old woman.

11:33.380 --> 11:34.730
Listen, Mamoru!

11:34.730 --> 11:37.500
Today, the two of us need to go to Rainbow Cape.

11:37.500 --> 11:39.280
Right, Ayako-san.

11:39.280 --> 11:42.270
But shouldn’t we just head off and go?

11:42.270 --> 11:46.200
No. They’ll notice, and they’ll come make fun of us!

11:46.200 --> 11:47.690
That’s what they do.

11:48.550 --> 11:51.960
We need to head out without being noticed.

11:51.960 --> 11:53.060
Right.

11:55.110 --> 11:57.830
Now, let’s go shopping!

11:57.830 --> 11:59.170
Yeah.

11:59.170 --> 12:01.070
Give me this.

12:03.040 --> 12:04.970
This, this, look at this!

12:08.340 --> 12:10.740
It’s going to be hard...

12:10.740 --> 12:12.750
to just sneak off.

12:13.270 --> 12:16.880
By the way, you haven’t bought
anything yet, have you, Emelenzia-san?

12:16.880 --> 12:18.610
No, I...

12:18.610 --> 12:21.920
We don’t often get to take trips like this,
so buy some clothes or something!

12:21.920 --> 12:23.180
That’s right.

12:23.180 --> 12:25.630
I’ll pick some out for you.

12:25.630 --> 12:26.910
No. No, you won’t.

12:27.500 --> 12:29.030
Let’s go.

12:29.030 --> 12:30.660
No, I don’t need...

12:30.660 --> 12:32.700
Come on, don’t be that way.

12:33.770 --> 12:35.060
Ayako-san!

12:35.060 --> 12:35.650
Yeah!

12:36.040 --> 12:37.610
This is our chance!

12:39.090 --> 12:40.520
This is going to work.

12:40.520 --> 12:41.310
Right.

12:44.450 --> 12:49.960
Now that I’ve learned
Naoyuki-style street fighting, you can’t fool me.

12:49.960 --> 12:51.970
You can’t!

12:51.970 --> 12:54.330
Abiko-sempai, wh-why are you...

12:54.930 --> 12:56.420
I see.

12:57.430 --> 12:58.860
No, Ayako-san!

12:58.860 --> 13:00.430
Not here!

13:03.330 --> 13:04.760
Ta-dah!

13:08.640 --> 13:10.830
So cute, Emelenzia-san!

13:10.830 --> 13:11.710
Yeah, huh?

13:11.710 --> 13:13.560
I picked it out, and I’m surprised, too.

13:13.560 --> 13:14.980
You’re amazing!

13:15.570 --> 13:19.920
This is sure to be better!

13:19.920 --> 13:20.820
No.

13:21.530 --> 13:22.840
Emelenzia-san!

13:26.310 --> 13:28.470
OK, everyone applaud!

13:53.680 --> 13:54.950
What should we do?

13:54.950 --> 13:58.940
At this rate, we won’t be able to go alone.

13:58.940 --> 13:59.610
No!

14:02.250 --> 14:03.060
Um...

14:03.650 --> 14:09.430
I was happy that you invited me to go...

14:10.350 --> 14:11.500
So...

14:13.120 --> 14:16.420
Me, too, Ayako-san.

14:16.910 --> 14:19.010
But with this situation...

14:21.520 --> 14:22.420
Mister!

14:22.420 --> 14:23.360
Miss!

14:26.570 --> 14:28.050
Hi!

14:28.050 --> 14:29.370
You’re...

14:29.370 --> 14:30.510
Mary!

14:30.510 --> 14:34.020
You’re boyfriend and girlfriend!

14:34.020 --> 14:36.830
Don’t you want to be alone?

14:38.020 --> 14:39.600
Um...

14:40.390 --> 14:42.450
That’s right, but...

14:42.450 --> 14:43.370
Ayako-san!

14:46.610 --> 14:47.860
Here’s something to drink.

14:49.280 --> 14:50.600
Thank you.

14:50.600 --> 14:51.870
You’re welcome.

14:52.720 --> 14:53.780
Having fun?

14:54.120 --> 14:56.450
Yes. A lot!

14:56.450 --> 14:57.700
Glad to hear it.

14:58.180 --> 15:00.990
Um... Thank you.

15:03.040 --> 15:07.220
I don’t think I’ve ever had this much fun.

15:07.670 --> 15:08.590
Yeah?

15:08.920 --> 15:12.220
Everyone’s so nice to me.

15:12.220 --> 15:14.200
Ever since I’ve been in Japan...

15:14.200 --> 15:17.850
No, even when I was in Germany, it wasn’t like this.

15:18.220 --> 15:19.460
Why?

15:20.060 --> 15:21.960
Why is this...

15:22.690 --> 15:23.740
Emelenzia-san!

15:24.410 --> 15:28.010
I heard about Ayako and Mamoru-san!

15:28.690 --> 15:31.510
You’re the one who pushed him on, huh?

15:31.510 --> 15:33.520
During that whole engagement thing.

15:33.520 --> 15:36.250
You were the one who told him to get a hold of himself.

15:36.740 --> 15:38.270
Pretty nice!

15:38.270 --> 15:39.290
So cool!

15:39.290 --> 15:40.920
I’m impressed.

15:42.270 --> 15:43.840
Shione!

15:43.840 --> 15:47.380
N-No... That’s not true.

15:47.380 --> 15:49.540
That wasn’t it.

15:49.540 --> 15:51.770
I... I...

15:53.190 --> 15:54.140
Emelenzia-kun!

15:54.140 --> 15:54.850
What?

15:57.220 --> 15:58.740
She gets embarrassed.

15:59.480 --> 16:02.420
Emelenzia-san didn’t eat much!

16:02.900 --> 16:05.580
Then let’s bring her something later.

16:09.720 --> 16:12.090
No! No!

16:12.090 --> 16:16.090
It wasn’t for Mamoru or Witch Beatrice...

16:16.940 --> 16:20.130
I couldn’t just say nothing!

16:20.130 --> 16:24.250
I couldn’t just watch them suffer!

16:27.130 --> 16:28.870
<i>Why is this?</i>

16:28.870 --> 16:32.530
<i>When they’re miserable, so is my heart...</i>

16:33.240 --> 16:36.600
<i>But even when I see them happy, my heart still...</i>

16:37.900 --> 16:41.420
<i>Even when my brother sought Witch Beatrice...</i>

16:41.420 --> 16:44.350
<i>No, it wasn’t like this.</i>

16:44.910 --> 16:51.240
<i>When Witch Beatrice is by Mamoru, I... I...</i>

16:55.990 --> 16:58.720
<i>What is this pain?</i>

16:59.380 --> 17:03.960
<i>Brother, what is wrong with me?</i>

17:06.020 --> 17:07.050
This way!

17:07.050 --> 17:07.950
It’s this way.

17:07.950 --> 17:10.500
Looks like we made it out.

17:10.500 --> 17:13.780
Yes, now all we need to do
is get rid of Abiko-sempai.

17:14.900 --> 17:19.660
<i>You two want to go to the Rainbow Cape all alone!</i>

17:20.320 --> 17:22.630
<i>That’s right...</i>

17:22.630 --> 17:24.900
<i>But there’s a bother in the way.</i>

17:25.770 --> 17:28.810
<i>I know this hotel well.</i>

17:28.810 --> 17:30.830
<i>Like corridors only the staff know about.</i>

17:30.830 --> 17:32.530
<i>We can use them to get rid of him!</i>

17:37.820 --> 17:39.620
Here!

17:40.580 --> 17:42.200
Hurry!

17:42.200 --> 17:43.120
OK...

17:43.120 --> 17:48.300
I’ll watch, and once the bother
has passed, I’ll follow you!

17:48.300 --> 17:49.790
Thank you!

17:52.590 --> 17:55.660
Now, come out bad boy.

17:55.660 --> 17:58.740
I’ll give you punishment...

18:02.620 --> 18:06.810
I’m impressed you didn’t think you’d lost me.

18:06.810 --> 18:07.850
But!

18:07.850 --> 18:11.610
Do you really think you can punish me?

18:11.610 --> 18:13.550
I’m boiling mad.

18:13.550 --> 18:18.950
I’ll show this brat how harsh the adult world can be!

18:20.180 --> 18:22.280
Gotcha!

18:22.280 --> 18:25.910
<i>Naoyuki-style Street Fighting Super Move:</i>

18:26.240 --> 18:29.020
<i>Midair Explosion Fist! Beautiful Flowers!</i>

18:29.020 --> 18:31.630
Take this!

18:46.710 --> 18:50.080
What is that woman going to do?

18:53.490 --> 18:54.560
Mary-chan!

18:54.560 --> 18:56.110
Sorry to make you wait!

18:56.460 --> 18:59.300
The bother is gone now. Very gone.

19:00.180 --> 19:02.900
Now follow this path to the Rainbow Cape!

19:02.900 --> 19:03.560
OK!

19:03.560 --> 19:06.360
The only other worry is the weather.

19:06.910 --> 19:09.540
There are lots of rain clouds gathering...

19:09.540 --> 19:11.000
It’s OK.

19:13.240 --> 19:14.590
Ayako-san?

19:15.760 --> 19:16.770
I see...

19:16.770 --> 19:20.600
Yes, I stopped the clouds with beatrice.

19:20.600 --> 19:22.970
I told you I’d beat up anyone who got in our way.

19:23.800 --> 19:25.850
You’re amazing, Ayako-san.

19:26.180 --> 19:27.880
Take this, miss.

19:27.880 --> 19:29.480
What’s this?

19:29.900 --> 19:31.790
A happy item!

19:31.790 --> 19:35.730
Take it to the Rainbow Cape,
and you can be even happier!

19:36.650 --> 19:38.490
What do you think, Mamoru?

19:38.810 --> 19:40.960
It looks good, Ayako-san.

19:42.220 --> 19:43.330
Thank you!

19:45.210 --> 19:48.100
We can finally go to the Rainbow Cape.

19:48.100 --> 19:49.170
Right.

19:49.170 --> 19:52.320
But I don’t think we’ll see the rainbows.

19:52.320 --> 19:53.580
Yeah.

19:54.280 --> 20:00.010
But if I’m with you, that’s enough...

20:00.520 --> 20:01.750
Ayako-san.

20:23.700 --> 20:25.870
Come on, mister, miss!

20:25.870 --> 20:29.180
Once we’re through this cave,
we’ll be at the Rainbow Cape!

20:33.890 --> 20:35.150
It’s raining!

20:35.150 --> 20:38.180
No, I stopped it with beatrice!

20:38.180 --> 20:39.990
Let’s hurry, Ayako-san.

20:39.990 --> 20:41.120
Be careful!

20:41.120 --> 20:42.610
Thanks, Mary-chan!

20:42.610 --> 20:43.510
Thanks!

20:43.910 --> 20:45.400
Bye!

20:57.470 --> 20:58.540
An earthquake?

20:58.540 --> 20:59.640
Why, at a time like this?

20:59.640 --> 21:01.160
Let’s hurry!

21:01.760 --> 21:03.450
Ayako-san, the exit!

21:05.320 --> 21:07.470
We can’t go forward, Mamoru!

21:07.470 --> 21:08.550
Right!

21:23.400 --> 21:24.100
Ayako-san!

21:24.100 --> 21:25.140
Mamoru!

22:01.290 --> 22:06.970
My heart is racing and I'm going to give you

22:06.970 --> 22:12.170
This sparkling emotion

22:12.560 --> 22:18.300
The evening color is dyed into this orange shirt

22:18.360 --> 22:23.450
I catch it from behind you and my heart throbbing

22:23.560 --> 22:30.410
It's an everyday thrill just to be with you

22:30.410 --> 22:37.840
I can't say it well enough but thank you

22:37.840 --> 22:43.040
Venus Dream the hidden power

22:43.040 --> 22:49.240
This feeling will change into that power

22:49.240 --> 22:54.360
Power Dream I found what I want to protect

22:54.360 --> 23:00.770
That is your smile and your feelings

23:15.340 --> 23:19.700
If you asked me whether I prefer the sea or the mountains...

23:19.700 --> 23:21.490
Yeah...

23:21.490 --> 23:23.990
I suppose I’d say the mountains.

23:23.990 --> 23:26.860
The sea wind just clings to you, you know?

23:26.860 --> 23:28.570
And on the beach,

23:28.570 --> 23:34.900
it’s hard to walk past all the guys staring at my hot body.

23:35.370 --> 23:36.570
Sigh.

23:36.570 --> 23:38.710
Beauty is a sin.

23:39.560 --> 23:43.980
In a Storm

23:39.830 --> 23:42.490
Next time: In a Storm.
